\label{rem:context}
  If we have a derivation $\mathcal{D}$ from $A$ to $B$, and a context
  $G\coons{\cdot}R$, then we also have a derivation from
  $G\coons{A}R$ to $G\coons{B}R$. We can write this derivation
  as
  \begin{equation*}
    \ods{G\coons{A}R}{G\coons{\mathcal{D}}R}{G\coons{B}R}{}
    \quad\mbox{or}\quad
    \od{\odh{
        G\Coons{\ods{A}{\mathcal{D}}{B}{}}R}}
  \end{equation*}
  If $\mathcal{D}$ consists of a single inference rule, we sometimes write
  (with a slight abuse of notation)
  \begin{equation}\label{eq:rule-context}
    \od{\odh{
        G\Coons{\od{\odi{\odh{A}}{\mathsf{r}}{B}{}}}R}}
    \qquad\mbox{as}\qquad
    \od{\odi{\odh{G\Coons{A}R}}{\mathsf{r}}{G\Coons{B}R}{}}
  \end{equation}

\begin{equation*}
    \ods{G\coons{A}R}{G\coons{\mathcal{D}}R}{G\coons{B}R}{}
    \quad\mbox{or}\quad
    \od{\odh{
        G\Coons{\ods{A}{\mathcal{D}}{B}{}}R}}
  \end{equation*}

\begin{equation}\label{eq:rule-context}
    \od{\odh{
        G\Coons{\od{\odi{\odh{A}}{\mathsf{r}}{B}{}}}R}}
    \qquad\mbox{as}\qquad
    \od{\odi{\odh{G\Coons{A}R}}{\mathsf{r}}{G\Coons{B}R}{}}
  \end{equation}

In order to ease readability of derivations, we will mostly omit
the isomorphism steps shown in~\eqref{eq:iso}, and use the
abbreviation~\eqref{eq:iso-}. This concerns also situations
as shown below left, which are written as shown below right:
\begin{equation}
  \label{eq:iso-rule}
  \od{\odi{\odo{\odi{\odh{A}
        }{\mathsf{r}_1}{B}{}
      }{\isom}{B'}{}
    }{\mathsf{r}_2}{C}{}}
  \qquad\leadsto\qquad
  \od{\odi{\odi{\odh{A}
      }{\mathsf{r}_1}{B}{}
    }{\mathsf{r}_2}{C}{}}
  \quad\mbox{or}\quad
  \od{\odi{\odi{\odh{A}
      }{\mathsf{r}_1}{B'}{}
    }{\mathsf{r}_2}{C}{}}
\end{equation}
In other words, in derivations, we consider graphs equal modulo
isomorphisms. In particular, for the length $\sizeof\mathcal{D}$ of a
derivation, we count only the inference steps that are not
isomorphisms. This abuse of notation is justified as these
isomorphisms can be permuted with all inference rules that we
discuss in this paper. Furthermore, when we draw the graphs as in
\eqref{eq:exup} below, the isomorphisms are not visible.

\begin{equation}
    \label{eq:iso-rule}
    \od{\odi{\odo{\odi{\odh{A}
          }{\mathsf{r}_1}{B}{}
        }{\isom}{B'}{}
      }{\mathsf{r}_2}{C}{}}
    \qquad\leadsto\qquad
    \od{\odi{\odi{\odh{A}
        }{\mathsf{r}_1}{B}{}
      }{\mathsf{r}_2}{C}{}}
    \quad\mbox{or}\quad
    \od{\odi{\odi{\odh{A}
        }{\mathsf{r}_1}{B'}{}
      }{\mathsf{r}_2}{C}{}}
  \end{equation}

