\label{cor:deduction}
  For all graphs $G$ and $H$, we have
  \begin{equation*}
    \proves[\mathsf{GS}]{G\multimap H}
    \iff
    \odv{\varnothing}{}{\cneg G\vlbin{\parr}H}{\mathsf{GS}}
    \iff
    \odv{\varnothing}{}{\cneg G\vlbin{\parr}H}{\mathsf{SGS}}
    \iff
    \odv{G}{}{H}{\mathsf{SGS}}
  \end{equation*}

\begin{equation*}
    \proves[\mathsf{GS}]{G\multimap H}
    \iff
    \odv{\varnothing}{}{\cneg G\vlbin{\parr}H}{\mathsf{GS}}
    \iff
    \odv{\varnothing}{}{\cneg G\vlbin{\parr}H}{\mathsf{SGS}}
    \iff
    \odv{G}{}{H}{\mathsf{SGS}}
  \end{equation*}

The first equivalence is just the definition of $\proves{}$. The
second equivalence follows from Theorem~\ref{thm:up}, and the last equivalence follows from the two derivations
